  "id": "emotional-development",
  "term": "emotional development",
  "definition": "Emotional development is the growth of a child’s inner emotional capacities, including emotional autonomy, empathic expression, and the ability to adapt socially. In this packet, it is described as something that can be weakened when parenting creates hidden emotional pressure, leading a child to seem outwardly compliant while internally showing distress, inhibition, anxiety, or reduced sense of agency.",
